From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bjarne <87858321+bjakra@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 19:35:53 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gmscompat: optional keybox for sandboxed Play services' key
 attestation

AndroidKeyStoreSpi hands attestation chains to PlayKeyboxHooks, which only acts in the
unprivileged, signature-verified Play services process (GmsCompat enabled and PackageId.GMS_CORE).
It sends the chain to GmsCompatApp (new IGms2Gca.rewriteAttestationChain), which re-signs the
attested leaf with the user's keybox if they enabled one. The private key never leaves GmsCompatApp.
The returned leaf must keep the original public key and attestation extension; anything else, and
every other process, gets the stock chain. getCertificate() follows the rewritten chain.

PlayKeybox parses the common AndroidAttestation keybox XML strictly (EC and RSA, SEC1/PKCS#1/PKCS#8
PEM, complete chain to a self-signed root, matching private key) and does the re-signing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
